\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{2-\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/state.json" "file_sha256" "31710d2c7ffd1f9d9081e048833f4c1b154f9f477e209030e29e66492e86d933"} {"question" "q-76256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the row operations to $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{2-\\text{i}}{1+2\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ -2+\\text{i}+\\frac{(2-\\text{i})(1+2\\text{i})}{1+2\\text{i}} & \\text{i}+\\frac{(2-\\text{i})(1+\\text{i})}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{(\\text{i}-2)+(3+\\text{i})}{1+2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result  is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/state.json" "file_sha256" "31710d2c7ffd1f9d9081e048833f4c1b154f9f477e209030e29e66492e86d933"} {"question" "q-76256" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "37ba5df55475007f46a653df2e9ada705233f87b3c21410d3cbcfaa3ff4acf79"} {"question" "q-76256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/state.json" "file_sha256" "31710d2c7ffd1f9d9081e048833f4c1b154f9f477e209030e29e66492e86d933"} {"question" "q-76256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & \\text{i}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1-2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/state.json" "file_sha256" "31710d2c7ffd1f9d9081e048833f4c1b154f9f477e209030e29e66492e86d933"} {"question" "q-76256" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/state.json" "file_sha256" "31710d2c7ffd1f9d9081e048833f4c1b154f9f477e209030e29e66492e86d933"} {"question" "e-5903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $B=\\overline{A},$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/25ce0cd375da320d1615cf49f659ec33e4646cf6bc66455198bec5fd591b3dd3.png) What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5903.json" "file_sha256" "a598508fe345b33ab794eb90a8adef58179f36570555c0adff22f4fe85045a83"} {"question" "e-5903" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}4\\text{i} & 3-\\text{i} & 1+\\text{i} \\\\ 2-2\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 1+2\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 3\\text{i} & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1+2\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\text{i} & 3+\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 1-2\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -3\\text{i} & -2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5903.json" "file_sha256" "a598508fe345b33ab794eb90a8adef58179f36570555c0adff22f4fe85045a83"} {"question" "e-5525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/3e677aa7f2db1cc637e0566a60813ebae1e2bccf80325106317c1d2b7717c2a5.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/67a421166c674275ae14da43962c8e5c8ea37b6a9c8a0548d5b09428b703d831.png) are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/fde83769f627e95f5dfe3285bf275ebfe1678710a36c264b6662248063470bb0.png) then what is the value of $ad+eh?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5525.json" "file_sha256" "dca38b47609415927a6bb4500aa980bb412b8e74c89b3ffab25d357f3e4cf12a"} {"question" "e-5525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For the given matrix $A,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2-3\\text{i} & -5-7\\text{i} \\\\ 1-6\\text{i} & 5-9\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Re}(A)}+\\text{i}{{[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{\\text{Im}(A)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $a=2,d=5,e=-3$ and $h=-9.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5525.json" "file_sha256" "dca38b47609415927a6bb4500aa980bb412b8e74c89b3ffab25d357f3e4cf12a"} {"question" "e-5902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/b696bb055794a4ff94c86abc39ef3929113f82683b548a933fc1103245eff3fc.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/e6a5f5644ae4bcdfca4ca26bb258f33378381737ee036142c1e1c24f568ad2ed.png), then what is $AB?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5902.json" "file_sha256" "978194740b57b9a34adf68c5dccb46124ec9a9f6ae9001025476c91895702c94"} {"question" "e-5902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1+2\\text{i} & 1-\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(-\\text{i})\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & (-\\text{i})\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+\\text{i}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1\\cdot (1+2\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot \\text{i} & 1\\cdot (1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i}\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2-\\text{i})+(-1) & (-1-\\text{i})+2\\text{i} \\\\ (1+2\\text{i})+(-2) & (1-\\text{i})+4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1-\\text{i} & -1+\\text{i} \\\\ -1+2\\text{i} & 1+3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5902.json" "file_sha256" "978194740b57b9a34adf68c5dccb46124ec9a9f6ae9001025476c91895702c94"} {"question" "e-5526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given the matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/766ddf98a05c69ef0791858a7f32457425cf1a9650d2205227ffc7d9d173d2e7.png) find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\nR_1 := \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2 := R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5526.json" "file_sha256" "28c706e1816fe412e48cbda57827707f0de855165c7a3f724516c45deed62cf9"} {"question" "e-5526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's apply the row operations to $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\text{i}}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2+2\\text{i} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\, &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2\\text{i}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1+2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/assets/9fef320d53c15c2820719bb1d0dfabb00afa6200b43279e3137fbb25c4e67e2d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045065/example-5526.json" "file_sha256" "28c706e1816fe412e48cbda57827707f0de855165c7a3f724516c45deed62cf9"}] "usage" {"q-38392" [] "e-5902" [] "q-38397" [] "e-5526" [] "e-5903" [] "e-5525" [] "q-38391" [] "q-39014" []} "basis" 1666 "retractions" [[17592186129587 :question/problem "Find the real part of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 3\\textrm{i} & -5 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 6 - 7\\textrm{i} & 4 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186129584 :question/problem "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 - \\textrm{i} & 2 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 3 - 6\\textrm{i} & 3 - 3\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $x = \\begin{bmatrix}5 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + \\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$, then $Ax =$"] [17592186129585 :question/problem "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 + 3\\textrm{i} & 1 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + \\textrm{i} & 4 + 4\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 + 2\\textrm{i} & 2 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 2 + 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$, then $AB =$"] [17592186129647 :question/problem "Given the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}2\\textrm{i} - 1 & 0 \\\\ 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n\n$R_{1} = \\frac{1}{2\\textrm{i} - 1}R_{1}, R_{2} = R_{2} - 2\\textrm{i}R_{1}$"] [17592186128910 :question/problem "Find $B=\\overline{A}$, where $\\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} & 3 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i} & 2 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 3\\textrm{i} & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ What is the value of $b_{11} + b_{23}$?"] [17592186128910 :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA^(―) &= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} & 3 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i} & 2 - \\textrm{i} & 1 + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 3\\textrm{i} & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}^(―) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i}^(―) & 3 - \\textrm{i}^(―) & 1 + \\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ 2 - 2\\textrm{i}^(―) & 2 - \\textrm{i}^(―) & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ \\textrm{i}^(―) & 3\\textrm{i}^(―) & 2\\textrm{i}^(―)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} & 3 + \\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 2 + \\textrm{i} & 1 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ -\\textrm{i} & -3\\textrm{i} & -2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nb_{11} + b_{23} = (-4\\textrm{i}) + (1-2\\textrm{i}) = 1-6\\textrm{i}\n$$"] [17592186128880 :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}e & f \\\\ g & h\\end{bmatrix}$ are the real and imaginary parts of the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3\\textrm{i} & -5 - 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 - 6\\textrm{i} & 5 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is the value of $ad+eh$?"] [17592186128880 :question/worked-solution "For the given matrix $A$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3\\textrm{i} & -5 - 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 - 6\\textrm{i} & 5 - 9\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Re(A)) + \\textrm{i}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Im(A))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\na=2,d=5,e=-3\n$$\n\nand $h=-9$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nad+eh=2 \\cdot 5 + (-3) \\cdot (-9) = 37\n$$"] [17592186128909 :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}-\\textrm{i} & \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 2\\end{bmatrix}$, then what is $AB$?"] [17592186128909 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the matrices using the usual method, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}-\\textrm{i} & \\textrm{i} \\\\ 1 & 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 - \\textrm{i} \\\\ \\textrm{i} & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}(-\\textrm{i}) \\cdot (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + \\textrm{i} \\cdot \\textrm{i} & (-\\textrm{i}) \\cdot (1 - \\textrm{i}) + \\textrm{i} \\cdot 2 \\\\ 1 \\cdot (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\cdot \\textrm{i} & 1 \\cdot (1 - \\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}(2 - \\textrm{i}) + (-1) & (-1 - \\textrm{i}) + 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ (1 + 2\\textrm{i}) + (-2) & (1 - \\textrm{i}) + 4\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 - \\textrm{i} & -1 + \\textrm{i} \\\\ -1 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1 + 3\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128881 :question/problem "Given the matrix $\\begin{bmatrix}\\textrm{i} & -\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ find the result of applying to $A$ the following elementary row operations:\n$R_1:= \\dfrac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_1, \\qquad R_2:= R_2 - 2\\textrm{i}R_1$"] [17592186128881 :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the row operations to $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\textrm{i} & -\\textrm{i} \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1}:=\\frac{1}{\\textrm{i}}R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 + 2\\textrm{i} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2\\textrm{i}R_{1} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the result is\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 + 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186127299 17592186127300 17592186127301 17592186127302 17592186127303 17592186127305 17592186127306 17592186127307 17592186127308 17592186127309 17592186127317 17592186127318 17592186127319 17592186127320 17592186127321 17592186127677 17592186127678 17592186127679 17592186127680 17592186127681] "immutable_fields" [[17592186127298 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127298 :answer-field/id] [17592186127298 :answer-field/key] [17592186127298 :answer-field/type] [17592186127304 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127304 :answer-field/id] [17592186127304 :answer-field/key] [17592186127304 :answer-field/type] [17592186127316 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127316 :answer-field/id] [17592186127316 :answer-field/key] [17592186127316 :answer-field/type] [17592186127676 :answer-field/correct] [17592186127676 :answer-field/id] [17592186127676 :answer-field/key] [17592186127676 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
